.PP
\fBFlowGrid\fR: items of equal size that flow into columns, after Mantine's \fBSimpleGrid\fR. Either a fixed number of columns (\fBcols\fR: one column is a list) or as many as fit, each at most \fBmax_width\fR wide. The items fill their cells and keep their own height (a row is as tall as its tallest item). Albums, playlists, apps, projects.
.PP
A thin, named form of iced's \fBGrid\fR, with the sizing that suits items. When cells should differ in width, use a \fBTableGrid\fR.
.PP
.nf
.RS
FlowGrid::new(albums.iter().map(album_card)).max_width(180.0)
FlowGrid::new(albums.iter().map(album_row)).cols(1)   // a list
.RE
